  "live_records": {
    "q-105791": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105791",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\times (4F+G)$ at the point $(0,1,-1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+xz\\,j+(y-1)\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=z\\,i.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =∇\\times (4F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4∇\\times F+∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ y{e}^{x} & xz & y-1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xz)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-1)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(y{e}^{x})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xz)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y{e}^{x})]k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i-(0-0)\\,j+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k \\\\  & =(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (4F+G) & =4(∇\\times F)+∇\\times G \\\\  & =4[(1-x)\\,i+(z-{e}^{x})\\,k]+z\\,i \\\\  & =4(1-x)\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k+z\\,i \\\\  & =[4(1-x)+z]\\,i+4(z-{e}^{x})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,1,-1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (4F+G))(0,1,-1) & =[4(1-0)+(-1)]\\,i+4(-1-{e}^{0})\\,k \\\\  & =[4-1]\\,i+4(-1-1)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\,i-8\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
