    "q-105796": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105796",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\times (F+G)$ at the point $(0,-1,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i+3z\\,j-2y\\,\\text{k},\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=(6z-1)\\,j.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & 3z & -2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3z)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3z)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]k \\\\  & =(-2-3)i-(0-0)j+(0-0)k \\\\  & =-5\\,i.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times G \\\\  & =-5\\,i+(6z-1)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(0,-1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F+G))(0,-1,1) & =-5\\,i+(6(1)-1)\\,j \\\\  & =-5\\,i+5\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
