    "q-41898": {
      "dom_id": "step-q41898",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\times (F+2G)$ at the point $(1,1,1)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+{x}^{2}y\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)={x}^{2}z\\,i+(xy-2xyz)\\,j-xz\\,k.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+2G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (2G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F+2∇\\times G\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ {x}^{2}z & 0 & {x}^{2}y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(0)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}z)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(0)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}z)]k \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-0)i-(2xy-{x}^{2})j+(0-0)k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F+2G) & =∇\\times F+2∇\\times G \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy)\\,j+2[{x}^{2}z\\,i+(xy-2xyz)\\,j-xz\\,k] \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-2xy+2xy-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(1+2z)\\,i+({x}^{2}-4xyz)\\,j-2xz\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(1,1,1),$ we get\n\n$$\n(∇\\times (F+2G))(1,1,1)=3\\,i-3\\,j-2\\,k.\n$$",
