    "q-105798": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105798",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\times (F-G)$ at the point $(-2,0,3)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=z{e}^{y}\\,i+3\\,j-x\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ z{e}^{y} & 3 & -x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-x)-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{e}^{y})]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{e}^{y})]k \\\\  & =(0-0)i-((-1)-{e}^{y})j+(0-z{e}^{y})k \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-G) & =∇\\times F-∇\\times G \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-[2x{e}^{y}\\,i-2{e}^{y}\\,j] \\\\  & =({e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+2{e}^{y}\\,j \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{y}\\,i+(3{e}^{y}+1)\\,j-z{e}^{y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(-2,0,3),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-G))(-2,0,3) & =-2(-2){e}^{0}\\,i+(3{e}^{0}+1)\\,j-3{e}^{0}\\,k \\\\  & =4\\,i+4\\,j-3\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
