    "q-105795": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105795",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Calculate $∇\\times (F-3G)$ at the point $(1,0,9)$ for the vector fields $F$ and $G,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=(2\\sqrt{z}+x)\\,i+xy\\,j+{y}^{2}\\,k,\\,(∇\\times G)(x,y,z)=3{x}^{2}y\\,k.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following linearity properties for curl:\n\n- $∇\\times (kF)=k∇\\times F$\n\n- $∇\\times (F+G)=∇\\times F+∇\\times G$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-3G) & =∇\\times F+∇\\times (-3G) \\\\  & =∇\\times F-3∇\\times G.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $∇\\times F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x} & \\frac{∂}{∂y} & \\frac{∂}{∂z} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{z}+x & xy & {y}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy)]i-[\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})-\\frac{∂}{∂z}(2\\sqrt{z}+x)]j+[\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy)-\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\sqrt{z}+x)]k \\\\  & =(2y-0)i-(0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}})j+(y-0)k \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (F-3G) & =∇\\times F-3∇\\times G \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k-3[3{x}^{2}y\\,k] \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y\\,k-9{x}^{2}y\\,k \\\\  & =2y\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{z}}\\,j+y(1-9{x}^{2})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, evaluating at the point $(1,0,9),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(∇\\times (F-3G))(1,0,9) & =2(0)\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}}\\,j+0(1-9(1)^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
