    "q-105964": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105964",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨3z,2x,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=xz+y.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,3,2⟩,\\,∇f=⟨z,1,x⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(1,0,0).$",
      "worked_solution": "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ z & 1 & x \\\\ 3z & 2x & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[1(0)-x(2x)]i-[z(0)-x(3z)]j+[z(2x)-1(3z)]k \\\\  & =-2{x}^{2}\\,i+3xz\\,j+(2xz-3z)\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(xz+y)⟨0,3,2⟩+⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,3(xz+y),2(xz+y)⟩+⟨-2{x}^{2},3xz,2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},3(xz+y)+3xz,2(xz+y)+2xz-3z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{x}^{2},6xz+3y,4xz+2y-3z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(1,0,0) & =⟨-2(1)^{2},6(1)(0)+3(0),4(1)(0)+2(0)-3(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
