    "q-105956": {
      "dom_id": "step-q105956",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z,\\sqrt{x},0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=-z.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,0,-1⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(4,1,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ z & \\sqrt{x} & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[0(0)-(-1)(\\sqrt{x})]i-[0(0)-(-1)(z)]j+[0(\\sqrt{x})-0(z)]k \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\,i-z\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(-z)⟨0,1,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩+⟨\\sqrt{x},-z,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{x},-2z,-\\frac{z}{2\\sqrt{x}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(4,1,4) & =⟨\\sqrt{4},-2(4),-\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{4}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-8,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
