    "q-131475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131475",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨x{e}^{y},yz,0⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{-y}.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨-y,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩,\\,∇f=⟨{e}^{-y},-x{e}^{-y},0⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,1,2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {e}^{-y} & -x{e}^{-y} & 0 \\\\ x{e}^{y} & yz & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[(-x{e}^{-y})(0)-(yz)(0)]i-[({e}^{-y})(0)-(x{e}^{y})(0)]j+[({e}^{-y})(yz)-(x{e}^{y})(-x{e}^{-y})]k \\\\  & =0\\,i+0j+(yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2})k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =(x{e}^{-y})⟨-y,0,-x{e}^{y}⟩+⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-xy{e}^{-y},0,-{x}^{2}⟩+⟨0,0,yz{e}^{-y}+{x}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-xy{e}^{-y},0,yz{e}^{-y}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,1,2)=⟨0,0,\\frac{2}{e}⟩.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131475-a",
